= Citations

Where the book leans on work outside it, chiefly on consciousness, which the
chapter on knowledge reaches and then stops at: Annaka Harris on consciousness
as possibly fundamental rather than emergent, David Chalmers on the hard
problem, Anil Seth, Giulio Tononi on integrated information theory, and Thomas
Metzinger.
